proposed_comments.body:
### Restore the send guard when worker startup fails

**Severity:** `medium`

`_sendInProgress` is set before constructing and starting the worker. If either startup step throws, `Send` never runs its `finally`, so the flag remains set and subsequent calls skip injection indefinitely. Reset the guard on this startup-failure path, then rethrow rather than swallowing the startup exception.

**Suggested change:**
```suggestion
            try
            {
                var sendThread = new Thread(Send)
                {
                    IsBackground = true,
                    Name = "PowerToys foreground input",
                };
                sendThread.Start();
            }
            catch
            {
                Volatile.Write(ref _sendInProgress, 0);
                throw;
            }
```

Verify a simulated failure before the first start clears the guard and a subsequent real thread start succeeds; retain the normal send/finally behavior.

### Skip foreground input for a zero window handle (1/2)

**Severity:** `medium`

The public overload routes here. With `IntPtr.Zero`, the existing already-foreground guard is skipped, so the method injects synthetic input and then calls foreground APIs even though zero cannot identify a window. Return before either side effect.

**Suggested change:**
```suggestion
            if (handle == IntPtr.Zero)
            {
                return;
            }

            // There's no foreground lock to get past if the window is already in the foreground, so don't send input.
```

Apply with the fixture update (2/2). Verify a zero-handle call through the fake-injector overload returns without invoking the injected action; keep the nonzero foreground path unchanged.

### Preserve fake-input coverage with the zero-handle guard (2/2)

**Severity:** `medium`

The fake-input tests use `NoWindow` to exercise the injection path without a real window. After adding the shared zero-handle return (1/2), zero would skip that path and invalidate the off-caller and STA non-pumping assertions. Use a nonzero invalid HWND for those existing tests. A zero-handle regression should instead pass `IntPtr.Zero` and assert that its fake injector is not called.

```suggestion
    // Minus one is not a window, so the real SetForegroundWindow/AttachThreadInput calls that
    // BringToForeground makes after the faked input fail without touching the desktop.
    private static readonly IntPtr NoWindow = new(-1);
```

Apply only with (1/2), then run the fake-injector zero-handle, off-caller and STA non-pumping cases.

